  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Hani Berzi is an Egyptian food entrepreneur who co-founded Edita, a producer of packaged sweet snacks, with partners including his family’s investment company. An engineering graduate of Ain Shams University, he began in the family’s Tasty Foods business, established food distributor Digma and became Edita’s group chairman and chief executive.",
    "html": "<p>Hani Berzi is an Egyptian food entrepreneur who co-founded Edita, a producer of packaged sweet snacks, with partners including his family’s investment company. An engineering graduate of Ain Shams University, he began in the family’s Tasty Foods business, established food distributor Digma and became Edita’s group chairman and chief executive.</p>\r\n",
    "word_count": 50,
    "confidence": {
      "score": 94,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Primary corporate history and firsthand interviews support material text."
    },
    "source_ids": [
