    ]
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Food entrepreneur Hani Berzi backed packaged croissants when potential customers in Egypt were unfamiliar with the product, which he had encountered on a visit to Greece. Despite discouragement, he introduced the chocolate-filled Molto range and positioned it as an affordable everyday snack. Cakes offered a further opportunity because they used similar ingredients, allowing Edita to extend its range into another part of the snack market.\n\nPreparing younger relatives to work in the business also received a formal structure. Through Edita’s Step programme, family members gain experience in different departments before shaping their involvement in the company.",
    "html": "<p>Food entrepreneur Hani Berzi backed packaged croissants when potential customers in Egypt were unfamiliar with the product, which he had encountered on a visit to Greece. Despite discouragement, he introduced the chocolate-filled Molto range and positioned it as an affordable everyday snack. Cakes offered a further opportunity because they used similar ingredients, allowing Edita to extend its range into another part of the snack market.</p>\r\n<p>Preparing younger relatives to work in the business also received a formal structure. Through Edita’s Step programme, family members gain experience in different departments before shaping their involvement in the company.</p>\r\n",
